DNS Resolver flow:
=================

Example.com --> Browser --> Browser Cache --> OS --> OS Cache --> ISP DNS Resolver --> ISP/DNS Cache --> Root Servers --> TLD Owners --> Registars(GoDaddy) --> fetches A record

Root servers  ==> 13 are there world wide and they handles internet with these.
Tracks all Domain information and TLD Information.

TLD Top Level Domain: 
.com
.in
.org
.us
.uk
.ai
etc..

Domain Registars/Sellers:  GoDaddy, Hostinger, aws, gcp, azure etc..

How to apply for a domain ==>
1. Availability check with TLD Owners is Domain available or not.
2. If available Collects the details from buyers.
3. After payments, GoDaddy updates details to TLD about buyer and details of domain.
4. Create A record against the domain.
   example.com A 17.18.19.212  ==> GoDaddy updates to TLD.

We can change authority to another company from Registars to have separate Name Servers to provide IP address.
Name Servers NS: handles internet requests of the domain

TTL : Time To Live in Cache, Min 1 hr 3600 sec to be set, if your domain updates are frequent we need to chane to min value to propagate updates to all places.
After updates we can re set to 3600 sec for better performance/optimisations.


nslookup -type=ns prashum.online
